    <string name="discovery_method_transit_explained">The star dimmed slightly each time the planet passed in front of it.</string>
    <string name="discovery_method_radial_velocity_explained">The planet\'s pull made its star wobble, shifting the colour of its light back and forth.</string>
    <string name="discovery_method_microlensing_explained">Its gravity briefly magnified the light of a more distant star lined up behind it.</string>
    <string name="discovery_method_imaging_explained">Telescopes photographed the planet itself, with the star\'s glare blocked out.</string>
    <string name="discovery_method_transit_timing_explained">It tugged on a known transiting planet, making its transits come early or late.</string>
    <string name="discovery_method_eclipse_timing_explained">It shifted the timing of the eclipses of the two stars it orbits.</string>
    <string name="discovery_method_orbital_brightness_explained">The star\'s brightness rose and fell with the planet\'s orbit as it reflected and heated.</string>
    <string name="discovery_method_pulsar_timing_explained">It disturbed the clock-like radio pulses of the dead star it orbits.</string>
    <string name="discovery_method_pulsation_timing_explained">It shifted the timing of its star\'s regular pulsations.</string>
    <string name="discovery_method_astrometry_explained">Precise positions showed the star tracing a tiny loop across the sky.</string>
    <string name="discovery_method_disk_kinematics_explained">It disturbed the motion of gas in the disk around a young star.</string>
    <string name="discovery_method_other_explained">Found by a method the archive does not classify further.</string>
